<title>USA: Vermont House okays longer hours for alcohol sales.</title>
<headline>Vermont House okays longer hours for alcohol sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Vermont House has approved legislation to extend the hours that alcohol could be sold in bars on Saturday nights.</p>
<p>Currently, bars can serve booze until 0200 EST six nights a week but only until 0100 on Saturday nights. That restriction on Saturday night is a remnant of the old &quot;Blue&quot; laws that restricted business activities on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Senate will now take the bill under consideration.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
